 "notes": "STRETCH 1. p.118 from the row below the long rule ('1. re en unt reṭ ...') to the foot (5 rows); p.119 all rows. LXXIV up to 'ḥetep' (p.119 row 2), VIII from the p.119 title. Line numerals: LXXIV '1.' before re (p.118 title row); '2.' before em (p.118 row 3, before Neter-χert); '3.' inside χu (between G25 and G43, p.118 row 4) so χu stays line 2, line 3 from à; '4.' inside ḥer at the end of p.118 row 5 (between D2/Z1 and D21) so ḥer stays line 3; p.119 rows 1-2 continue line 4. VIII: '1.' before the bracketed re (p.119 row 3); '2.' before ṭep (row 4); '3.' after Rā, before àtef (row 6); '4.' before the second àm (row 7). Overlines: no separate thin overline is printed; on both pages the long chapter rule runs over the title only as far as àn and stops just before Àusàr (p.118: x≈236-913 pt, Àusàr begins ≈923; p.119: x≈206-868, Àusàr ≈879). I have marked the title words and t'eṭ àn rubric:true on that basis - if the rule is only a separator, drop those flags. No overline over any other word. Dots printed: p.119 row 4 'ṭep ....' (transliteration) and row 5 '.... em' / 'splendours .... on' (transliteration and English). Brief quotes '[pert]' but Budge's transliteration prints 'pert' without brackets; the hieroglyph group and the English '[and of coming forth]' are bracketed. Brackets in hieroglyph line p.119: [re] row1; [re en] title; [pert] title; [nuk] row6; [àm] row6; [O4] and [G43 N5] in hru-f row7. No footnotes, no (sic)/(?) in this stretch. p.119 row 1 'àbeḥ' follows directly from p.118 row 5."
